        <td>{{ t.b26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.e26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.d26 | pct }}</td><td>{{ t.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
      {% set cv = C["La Jolla Cove"] %}{% set na = C["Nautilus"] %}
      <tr class="sep"><td class="dim">La Jolla Cove <small>(budget: remodels)</small></td><td class="dim">{{ cv.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.q4_b | fk }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.q4_o | fk }}</td>
        <td class="dim">{{ cv.b26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.e26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.d26 | pct }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Nautilus <small class="pink">(not in the budget)</small></td><td>{{ na.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ na.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.q4_o | fk }}</td>
        <td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.e26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note pin-bottom">Our finish = January–September Toast actuals + our models' October–December forecast. Budget columns come from the budget workbook; its January–September for Beverly Hills is {{ (C["Beverly Hills"].ytd26 - C["Beverly Hills"].b_ytd) | fk }} below Toast, so the columns do not add across for that café. Del Mar Café appears as Carmel Valley in Toast.</p>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 6 BRIDGE 2026 #}
{% set B = n.bridge26 %}{% set bmax = B.ours %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 1 · The 2026 finish") }}
  <h1>The only real 2026 gap is scope: Nautilus is not in the budget</h1>
  <p class="lede">The budget's total-company 2026 is {{ B.budget_total | fm }}; our finish for all eleven cafés is {{ B.ours | fm }}. {{ "%.0f" | format(B.nautilus / (B.ours - B.budget_total) * 100) }}% of the {{ (B.ours - B.budget_total) | fk }} difference is one café the budget leaves out.</p>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.5">
      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="r"><div class="what">Budget: nine existing cafés</div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ B.budget9 / bmax * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.budget9 | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ La Jolla Cove<small>in the budget, listed under remodels</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.cove / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%;background:var(--g400)"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.cove | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r tot"><div class="what">= Budget: total company</div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ B.budget_total / bmax * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.budget_total | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ Nautilus<small>trading all year; not in the budget</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.nautilus / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt pink">{{ B.nautilus | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ October–December estimates<small>our models vs the budget's rule, eleven cafés</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.diff / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%;background:var(--g400)"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.diff | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r tot final"><div class="what">= Our 2026 finish, all eleven cafés<small>Toast to September + our October–December forecast</small></div><div><div class="bar ours" style="width:100%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.ours | fm }}</div></div>
      </div>
