    <div class="col" style="flex:1.7">
      <table class="roomy">
        <thead><tr><th class="l">Café or line</th><th>Budget 2027</th><th>Suggested</th><th>Change</th><th class="l">Basis</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for s in n.nine %}{% set c = C[s] %}
          <tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ c.b27 | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ c.suggest | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (c.suggest - c.b27) | sfk if (c.suggest - c.b27) | abs > 1 else "—" }}</td>
            <td class="l">{% if c.verdict in ["defensible", "in_line"] %}<span class="dim">Keep the budget ({{ VERDICT_LABEL[c.verdict] | lower }})</span>{% else %}Our plan{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Nine existing cafés</td><td>{{ t.b27 | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.nine | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.nine_change | sfm }}</td><td class="l">{{ (S.nine / t.e26 - 1) | pct }} on 2026</td></tr>
          <tr class="sep"><td>Nautilus</td><td class="dim">—</td><td><b>{{ C["Nautilus"].plan27 | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ C["Nautilus"].plan27 | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Our plan; not in the budget</td></tr>
          <tr><td>La Jolla Cove</td><td>{{ cv.b27 | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ cv.plan27 | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (cv.plan27 - cv.b27) | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Current trend; add the remodel lift once it trades</td></tr>
          {% for x in O.new %}
          <tr><td>{{ x.name }}</td><td>{{ x.budget | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ x.track | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (x.track - x.budget) | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Our average opening, {{ x.months }} months</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Total company</td><td>{{ S.total_budget | fm }}</td><td class="pink">{{ S.total | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.total_change | sfm }}</td><td class="l">{{ S.total_g | pct }} on 2026</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <h3>How we got there</h3>
      <ul class="tight big">
        <li><b>Raise six objectives</b> to our plan: {{ S.raised | join(", ") }}.</li>
        <li><b>Keep three</b> where the budget's caution has support: {{ S.kept | join(", ") }}.</li>
        <li><b>Show judgment calls as their own lines</b>: competitors next door, the Cove remodel and openings beyond our track record are upside or risk, not the base.</li>
        <li><b>Re-forecast every month</b> as actuals land; the models update themselves.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout" style="margin-top:14px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:12px">Even the suggested {{ S.nine | fm }} for the nine cafés assumes growth slows from {{ t.g26 | apct(0) }} to {{ (S.nine / t.e26 - 1) | apct(0) }}.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 14 DIVIDER 3 + INDEX #}
<section class="page divider">
  <div class="div-left" style="padding-right:.5in">
    <div class="part">Part 3</div>
    <div class="div-title" style="font-size:44px">Café by café</div>
    <p class="div-sub" style="margin-bottom:16px">Two pages each: the numbers, then the evidence behind our read.</p>
    <table style="font-size:11.5px">
      <thead><tr><th class="l">Café</th><th>Budget</th><th>Our plan</th><th class="l">Our read</th><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for c in n.cafes %}
        <tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ (c.b27 | fm) if c.b27 else "—" }}</td><td>{{ c.plan27 | fm }}</td><td class="l">{{ badge(c.verdict) }}</td><td>{{ 16 + 2 * loop.index0 }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="div-right"><img src="assets/tout-mission.jpg" alt=""></div>
</section>

{# ================================================================== 15+ CAFÉ PAGES #}
{% for c in n.cafes %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Café by café · " ~ c.name ~ " · the numbers") }}
  <div class="cafe-tag"><span class="name">{{ c.name }}</span>{{ badge(c.verdict) }}</div>
  <h1>{{ c.h1 }}</h1>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.75">
      <div class="chart-title">Monthly net sales</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Actual to Sep 2026 · our forecast from Oct 2026 (dotted to Dec, then the 2027 plan){% if c.key == "La Jolla Cove" %} · budget 2027 = Jan–Sep 2026 repeated, then $125K a month{% elif c.b27 %} · budget 2027 = each 2026 month {{ c.bg | pct }}{% endif %}</div>
      {{ svg.cafe[c.key].monthly }}
    </div>
    <div class="col side" style="flex:1">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th class="l"></th><th>Budget</th><th>Ours</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2026 finish</td><td>{{ (c.b26 | fm) if c.b26 else "—" }}</td><td>{{ c.e26 | fm }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>2027</b></td><td><span class="num-big">{{ (c.b27 | fm) if c.b27 else "—" }}</span></td><td><span class="num-big pink">{{ c.plan27 | fm }}</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Growth on 2026</td><td>{{ (c.bg | pct) if c.b27 else "—" }}</td><td>{{ c.pg | pct }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Added in 2027</td><td>{{ (c.added27_b | sfk) if c.b27 else "—" }}</td><td>{{ c.added27_p | sfk }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Our three models</td><td></td><td>{{ c.low27 | frange(c.high27) }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="walk">
        <div><span>2025 actual</span><span>{{ c.fy25 | fm }}{% if c.g25 is not none %} ({{ c.g25 | pct }}){% endif %}</span></div>
        <div><span>Jan–Sep 2026 actual</span><span>{{ c.ytd26 | fm }} ({{ c.ytd_g | pct }})</span></div>
        <div><span>Oct–Dec 2026: budget · ours</span><span>{{ (c.q4_b | fk) if c.q4_b else "—" }} · {{ c.q4_o | fk }}</span></div>
        <div><span>Added in 2026</span><span>{{ c.added26 | sfk }}</span></div>
        {% if c.b27 %}<div><span>Our plan minus the budget, 2027</span><span class="{{ 'pink' if c.gap > 0 else '' }}">{{ c.gap | sfk }}</span></div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% if c.note %}<p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">{{ c.note }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

<section class="page">
  {{ head("Café by café · " ~ c.name ~ " · the evidence") }}
  <div class="cafe-tag"><span class="name">{{ c.name }}</span>{{ badge(c.verdict) }}</div>
  <h1>{{ c.h2 }}</h1>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.5">
      <div class="chart-title">Sales growth against the same quarter a year earlier</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Quarters since the café's first anniversary · gray bar: October 1–14, 2026 · dashed lines: 2027 growth{% if c.b27 %} in the budget and{% endif %} in our plan</div>
      {{ svg.cafe[c.key].quarterly }}
    </div>
    <div class="col says" style="flex:1">
      <h3>The budget says</h3>
      <p class="quote">{% if c.b27 %}“{{ c.key_assumption }}” · {{ c.bg | pct }}{% else %}Not included{% endif %}</p>
      <h3>The sales say</h3>
      <p>{{ c.says }}</p>
      <div class="minis">
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Guests (checks)<br>Jan–Sep vs 2025</div><div class="val">{{ c.chk_g | pct }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Average check<br>Jan–Sep vs 2025</div><div class="val">{{ c.tkt_g | pct }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Slowest quarter<br>on record</div><div class="val">{{ c.slowest | pct }}</div><div class="sub">{{ c.slowest_q }}</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="verdict pin-bottom">{{ badge(c.verdict) }}<span>{{ c.verdict_line }}</span></div>
  {{ foot("Quarterly growth from " ~ c.first_q ~ " · " ~ SRC) }}
</section>
{% endfor %}

{# ================================================================== METHOD #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("How we built our numbers") }}
  <h1>How we built our numbers</h1>
  <div class="row method" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="col">
      <h3>The data</h3>
      <p>Daily net sales and checks for every café from Toast POS (after discounts; excluding tax, tips and gift-card sales), {{ n.first_day.strftime("%B %Y") }} to {{ n.last_day.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") }}: {{ "{:,}".format(n.store_days) }} café-days.</p>
      <p>The budget's 2026 estimates match these figures within 2% café by café, so both sides are measuring the same sales.</p>
      <h3>Growth measures</h3>
      <p>Growth always compares the same days, months or quarters a year apart. Checks count guests' tickets; average check = net sales ÷ checks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>Our forecast</h3>
      <p>Three standard forecasting models (Prophet, SARIMA and Holt-Winters) are fitted to each café separately and added up. Their settings were tuned on 2025 and tested on January–September 2026.</p>
      <p><b>Our plan</b> is the blend of the three, shaded {{ "%.1f" | format((1 - n.plan_cfg.factor) * 100) }}% down: over-forecasting costs us about {{ n.plan_cfg.over_cost }}× more than under-forecasting, so the plan leans low on purpose.</p>
      <p><b>Track record:</b> forecasting January–September 2026 from September 2025, the blend came in {{ n.track.bias | apct }} {{ "below" if n.track.bias < 0 else "above" }} actual sales across the {{ n.track.cafes | words }} cafés with two years of history at the time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>What the models cannot see</h3>
      <p>New competitors, remodels, openings, closures and price changes. We treat these as judgment calls and show them as separate lines.</p>
      <h3>No growth after September</h3>
      <p>Two estimates of 2027 at today's level: Jul–Sep 2026 sales adjusted for each café's seasonal pattern and annualised; and each café's Prophet trend held at its September 30 level.</p>
      <h3>New-café track record</h3>
      <p>Sales in the first 8, 10 and 12 months from the first trading day of Newport, Beverly Hills, Brentwood and Carlsbad, restated at 2026 average checks.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="note pin-bottom">Budget figures come from the budget workbook (2027_Sales_budget_Investors.xlsx), imported by src/import_budget.py into data/cfo_budget_2027*.csv. Code: report/build_deck.py, src/hold_scenario.py. Café-level figures: outputs/budget_review_by_cafe.csv.</p>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

</body>
</html>
